# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/

# --- Anything that identifies the owner or their library -------------------
#
# This repo is code for reading a *personal* photo archive. Almost everything
# it produces at runtime is private, so the default is to ignore rather than to
# enumerate. If you add a file that holds archive content, add it here first.

# API keys and the Azure client id. `.env.example` is deliberately not ignored:
# it documents the keys with empty values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A live MSAL refresh token for the owner's OneDrive. Committing this hands
# over the account, not just the archive.
token-cache.json

# The archive itself: index.json plus photos/<yyyy-mm>.json. ~22MB here, and
# every record carries a filename, a OneDrive path, GPS coordinates, an AI
# caption and any transcribed text — so it is a searchable location history of
# the owner, not merely "generated data". Also covers data/jobs/ and
# data/bakeoff/.
data/

# Literal personal terms — the owner's name, and anything else they want caught
# by `redact`. The whole point of the file is that these strings cannot be found
# by pattern, which is exactly why they must not be published.
# See redaction-terms.example.json for the shape.
redaction-terms.json

# Exported trips. `Save as PDF` writes a self-contained document with the
# photographs embedded; one landing in the working tree must not be committed.
*.pdf

# Packaging output and staging. `staging/` holds the bundled pipeline server,
# `release/` the installer; both are rebuilt by `npm run package`. The icon in
# desktop/build/ IS committed — it is a source asset, not output.
desktop/release/
desktop/staging/

# Local editor/tool settings
*.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
